  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GAC -  Humanitarian WASH, Protection and Gender Response in Pibor and Akobo East</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ultimate outcome of the proposed project is reduced suffering, increased and maintained human dignity, and lives saved for conflict affected Internally Displaced Person (IDP) and host communities, particularly women, girls and people living with disabilities (PLWDs), in Greater Pibor Administrative Area (GPAA) and Akobo Counties of Jonglei State in South Sudan. Oxfam will accomplish this by improving access to gender -sensitive, safe, accessible Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services and enhancing the use of lifesaving Protection and Sexual and Gender Based Violence (SGBV) services in 9 target payams of GPAA and Akobo. All activities align with South Sudan&apos;s 2021 Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) and Humanitarian Needs Overview (HNO) priorities. The project strategy is informed by the cluster priorities, Oxfam assessment and Inter -agency assessment reports, also contributing to South Sudan&apos;s HRP for 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
